      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Tech giants claim that 'Right to Repair' laws would compromise their intellectual property and security, but this is a thinly veiled attempt to maintain their stranglehold on the market. In reality, the vast majority of devices have open-source or publicly available repair information, and third-party repairs have been done safely and effectively for decades. By using IP as a pretext, companies are trying to stifle competition and maintain their lucrative repair business, rather than prioritizing consumer choice and convenience.",
      "source": "target",
